### anomaly_detections

The anomaly_detections collection stores detection events generated by analytics, models, or rules. It supports status transitions, assignee tracking, and evidence objects that contribute to a decision. Entities refer to host, user, or device identifiers and link to related indicators when available.

Schema highlights:

- Required fields: _id, schema_version, created_at, updated_at, ingested_at, event_time, detection_rule_id_or_name, status, severity, entities[], confidence.
- Types: event_time timestamp; status enum; severity object; confidence int 0–100; entities array of objects; evidence array of objects; related_indicators array of indicator objects; references optional for investigation tickets.
- Extensions: model-specific details in a map.
- Idempotency: anomaly_id recommended for stable upserts.

Table 6: anomaly_detections Fields and Constraints

| Field/Subfield                         | Type            | Required | Validation Notes                                                                                   |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| schema_version                         | string          | Yes      | Non-empty string.                                                                                  |
| created_at, updated_at                 | timestamp       | Yes      | bsonType “date”.                                                                                   |
| ingested_at                            | timestamp       | Yes      | bsonType “date”.                                                                                   |
| event_time                             | timestamp       | Yes      | bsonType “date”.                                                                                   |
| anomaly_id                             | string          | No       | Stable ID for upsert; unique partial index candidate.                                              |
| detection_rule_id_or_name              | string          | Yes      | Non-empty.                                                                                         |
| status                                 | enum            | Yes      | “open”, “triage”, “investigating”, “resolved”, “false_positive”, “suppressed”.                     |
| severity                               | object          | Yes      | level enum; score int 0–100.                                                                       |
| confidence                             | int             | Yes      | 0–100 inclusive.                                                                                   |
| entities[]                             | object          | Yes      | type (enum: host, user, device), id (string), name (string), labels (array[string], optional).     |
| evidence[]                             | object          | No       | type (string), content (string), timestamp (timestamp), score (int, optional).                     |
| related_indicators[]                   | object          | No       | As in Table 3; optional linkage to indicators.                                                     |
| references[]                           | object          | No       | type enum; reference_id string; title/publisher optional.                                         |
| extensions                             | object          | No       | Model- or pipeline-specific details.                                                               |
| raw                                    | object          | No       | Optional snapshot of original detection event.                                                     |
| audit                                  | object          | No       | Audit metadata.                                                                                    |
| history                                | array[object]   | No       | Change tracking entries.                                                                           |

